.claude/
gocraft-linux-amd64
gocraft-windows-amd64.exe
*.exe
examples/go-plugin/bin/
# What `-gocraft-dump-commands` writes; the bundle build reads it and the
# packer skips it.
examples/go-plugin/.gocraft/
# `go build` with no -o names the binary after the directory.
examples/go-plugin/go-plugin

# The event generator, built at the root. *.exe covered the Windows build and
# nothing covered the one without an extension, which is how an 11 MB ELF got
# committed here once. Anchored: cmd/protoc-gen-gocraft is the source.
/protoc-gen-gocraft

# Same trap in the miniserv module: `go build ./...` there drops a 13 MB
# binary named after the directory, right next to its source.
/miniserv/miniserv

# Plugin bundles (.gcpkg files) dropped in by the admin.
# The README is tracked, so use the wildcard pattern instead of plugins/ to
# allow the negation rule below to work.
plugins/*
!plugins/README.md

# Worlds and state written by a running server
/world/
/world_nether/
/world_end/
logs/latest.log
logs/*.log.gz
ops.json
permissions.json
whitelist.json
banned-players.json
banned-ips.json
GoCraftWebsite
gocraft
im.png
